        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gabe Saporta, John S. Hall\n- Bands: Cobra Starship, King Missile\n- Works: The Body Has a Head\n- Places: New York City, New York, Germany\n\nFacts:\n- John S. Hall was born as John Charles Hall on September 2, 1960.\n- John S. Hall is an American poet, author, singer, and lawyer.\n- John S. Hall co-founded the avant-garde band King Missile in 1986 and has led it in various incarnations since then.\n- The album The Body Has a Head by King Missile frontman John S. Hall was released exclusively in Germany in 1996.\n- Gabe Saporta was born on October 11, 1979.\n- Gabe Saporta is a Uruguayan-American musician and entrepreneur.\n- Cobra Starship was created by former Midtown bassist and lead vocalist Gabe Saporta in 2006.\n- Cobra Starship was an American dance-pop band based in New York City, New York.",
